From nobody Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moleksy <moleksy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net/intel: assemble TX offload word in one store

ci_xmit_pkts() fills union ci_tx_offload one bitfield at a time. Each
assignment is a narrow read-modify-write of the stack copy, and the
whole word is then read back: by value in ci_txd_enable_checksum()
whenever a checksum offload is requested, and through the pointer in
the ice, i40e and idpf get_ctx_desc callbacks. That load overlaps
several pending narrow stores, store-to-load forwarding fails, and the
load waits for the stores to retire, once per packet.

Build the word in a register and store it once. The shifts follow the
layout the bitfields already have (l2_len 7, l3_len 9, l4_len 8,
tso_segsz 16, outer_l2_len 8, outer_l3_len 16 bits, from bit 0), and no
mbuf source field is wider than its slot, so the value is unchanged.
Re-check the shifts against union ci_tx_offload on every DPDK bump.

On an E810 VF with 2-segment ST 2110-20 packets (IPv4 checksum offload)
the stalled load was 21% of ci_xmit_pkts() cycles; one scheduler core
went from 8.06 to 8.66 Mpps.

MTL: drop once upstream DPDK fills the union with a single store.

Signed-off-by: moleksy <moleksy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/intel/common/tx_scalar.h | 13 +++++++------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/intel/common/tx_scalar.h b/drivers/net/intel/common/tx_scalar.h
--- a/drivers/net/intel/common/tx_scalar.h
+++ b/drivers/net/intel/common/tx_scalar.h
@@ -427,12 +427,13 @@
 		td_offset = (l2_len >> 1) << CI_TX_DESC_LEN_MACLEN_S;
 
 
-		tx_offload.l2_len = tx_pkt->l2_len;
-		tx_offload.l3_len = tx_pkt->l3_len;
-		tx_offload.outer_l2_len = tx_pkt->outer_l2_len;
-		tx_offload.outer_l3_len = tx_pkt->outer_l3_len;
-		tx_offload.l4_len = tx_pkt->l4_len;
-		tx_offload.tso_segsz = tx_pkt->tso_segsz;
+		/* one full-width store, so the whole-word reads below can forward from it */
+		tx_offload.data = (uint64_t)tx_pkt->l2_len |
+			((uint64_t)tx_pkt->l3_len << 7) |
+			((uint64_t)tx_pkt->l4_len << 16) |
+			((uint64_t)tx_pkt->tso_segsz << 24) |
+			((uint64_t)tx_pkt->outer_l2_len << 40) |
+			((uint64_t)tx_pkt->outer_l3_len << 48);
 
 		/* Calculate the number of context descriptors needed. */
 		nb_ctx = get_ctx_desc(ol_flags, tx_pkt, &tx_offload, txq, &cd_qw0, &cd_qw1);
